WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:06.200
Now before we jump in to creating our landscape material,

2
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.359
I wanna quickly talk about the landscape material slope.

3
00:00:10.359 --> 00:00:12.199
Now in this example here,

4
00:00:12.199 --> 00:00:15.519
we have taken a landscape material and broken it down

5
00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:17.000
to it's just basic components

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.039
so that we can highlight what is going on.

7
00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:24.039
And the landscape slope function works like this.

8
00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:27.660
When the slope or the angle of the terrain

9
00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.719
is between zero and 0.5 degrees,

10
00:00:30.719 --> 00:00:33.399
we're gonna show grass and then as we start to hit

11
00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:36.920
that 0.5, we're gonna slowly start to fade into dirt.

12
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:37.799
And we can see that right here,

13
00:00:37.799 --> 00:00:40.640
we have grass and then it's fading into dirt.

14
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.640
Now as that dirt angle goes from 0.5 all the way to one,

15
00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:50.439
we're then going to go from dirt into rock.

16
00:00:50.439 --> 00:00:52.479
And the coolest thing about this is again,

17
00:00:52.479 --> 00:00:56.039
as we lay out our terrain or we raise it

18
00:00:56.039 --> 00:00:58.320
or we lower it or we add features,

19
00:00:58.359 --> 00:01:01.539
instead of having to go in and repaint stuff,

20
00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:05.319
the material takes care of this for us automatically.

21
00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:07.500
And this is a huge time saver

22
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.799
because it allows us to spend more time

23
00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:12.620
manipulating the terrain and less time

24
00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.959
worrying about going back in and fixing things

25
00:01:14.959 --> 00:01:17.040
once we've done those manipulations.
